From 651f97b32f57aa431e938364116a8d33e8cff4a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:41:42 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(doctor): close the remaining argv secret gaps in holder
 descriptions

The argv mask behind hermes doctor's holder lists left known shapes out.
Now masked:
- random tokens of 16-19 characters (the bare-token floor was 20)
- letters-only random tokens: case flipping far more than camelCase does,
  or vowel-poor, with high entropy (repeated letters are not random)
- programs' own short password flags, keyed by the program: mysql/mariadb
  attached -pPASS, sshpass -p, redis-cli -a, openssl -k/-pass/-passin/
  -passout, curl -u/--user/--proxy-user user:pass, smbclient -U user%pass
- user:pass@host without a scheme
- a secret that starts with "-" after a secret-named flag
- secret-named command flags (--password-cmd, --api-key-helper): only the
  program is shown
- random segments posing as an UPPER_SNAKE name: most parts must be words
Kept, and tested: ssh -o options, -p as a port or Hermes profile, a bare
curl user, docker images, host:port, emails, git@host:repo, camelCase and
long lowercase words, nested --annotation=name=value values (judged under
their own name; a name may start with "_"). A live-process scan on the Mac
and an example gateway masks nothing besides macOS base64 service arguments.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
